--- title Conversion and text shaping
--- about AS reinterprets a value as a sibling type without copying, and
--- about the tab and line natives reshape text in place. The boundaries
--- about pinned here are what AS refuses and what the size refinements
--- about default to.

--- id text/making-a-pair-from-two-numbers
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold as-pair 1 2
--- result
"1x2"

--- id text/a-pair-from-a-fraction
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold as-pair 1.5 2
--- result
"1.5x2"

--- id text/a-pair-of-zeroes
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold as-pair 0 0
--- result
"0x0"

--- id text/a-pair-needs-numbers
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
as-pair "a" 1
--- error script expect-arg

--- id text/a-number-as-hex
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Padded to the full width of a whole number, and the answer is
--- note an issue rather than a string.
--- code
mold to-hex 255
--- result
"#00000000000000FF"

--- id text/zero-as-hex
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold to-hex 0
--- result
"#0000000000000000"

--- id text/a-negative-as-hex
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Two's complement rather than a minus sign.
--- code
mold to-hex -1
--- result
"#FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"

--- id text/hex-narrowed-to-a-width
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold to-hex/size 255 2
--- result
"#FF"

--- id text/spaces-become-a-tab
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Four spaces by default, which is not the eight a terminal
--- note usually means by a tab.
--- code
entab "    a"
--- result
"^-a"

--- id text/text-with-no-leading-spaces-is-unchanged
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
entab "a"
--- result
"a"

--- id text/a-tab-becomes-spaces
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
detab "^-a"
--- result
"    a"

--- id text/text-with-no-tabs-is-unchanged
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
detab "a"
--- result
"a"

--- id text/a-narrower-tab-stop
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
detab/size "^-a" 2
--- result
"  a"

--- id text/dropping-the-carriage-returns
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note DELINE turns the two-character line ending into the one-
--- note character one, which is what reading a file written elsewhere
--- note needs.
--- code
deline "a^M^/b"
--- result
"a^/b"

--- id text/a-block-reinterpreted-as-a-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note AS changes how a value is read without copying it. A block and
--- note a path hold the same thing and differ in how they are written.
--- code
b: [a b]
mold as path! b
--- result
"a/b"

--- id text/a-string-as-a-string-is-itself
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
as string! "a"
--- result
"a"

--- id text/a-block-cannot-be-read-as-a-string
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The two hold different things, so there is nothing to
--- note reinterpret. This is where AS stops and TO starts.
--- code
as block! "ab"
--- error script not-same-class
